mestre","ehl seh-MEHS-treh"],["course","el curso","ehl KOOR-soh"],["essay","el ensayo","ehl ehn-SAH-yoh"],["thesis","la tesis","lah TEH-sees"],["diploma","el título","ehl TEE-too-loh"],["seminar","el seminario","ehl seh-mee-NAH-ree-oh"],["entrance exam","el examen de acceso","ehl ehk-SAH-mehn deh ahk-SEH-soh"],["application","la solicitud","lah soh-lee-see-TOOD"],["student card","el carné de estudiante","ehl kahr-NEH deh ehs-too-dee-AHN-teh"]]},{"id":"school-verbs","title":"School verbs","items":[["to study","estudiar","ehs-too-dee-AR"],["to teach","enseñar","ehn-seh-NYAR"],["to ask","preguntar","preh-goon-TAR"],["to answer","responder","rehs-pohn-DEHR"],["to repeat","repetir","reh-peh-TEER"],["to understand","entender","ehn-tehn-DEHR"],["to remember","recordar","reh-kohr-DAR"],["to forget","olvidar","ohl-bee-DAR"],["to explain","explicar","ehks-plee-KAR"],["to practise","practicar","prahk-tee-KAR"],["to pass an exam","aprobar un examen","ah-proh-BAR oon ehk-SAH-mehn"],["to fail an exam","suspender un examen","soos-pehn-DEHR oon ehk-SAH-mehn"],["to write down","apuntar","ah-poon-TAR"],["to listen","escuchar","ehs-koo-CHAR"],["to read aloud","leer en voz alta","leh-EHR ehn bohs AHL-tah"],["to think","pensar","pehn-SAR"],["to count","contar","kohn-TAR"],["to spell","deletrear","deh-leh-treh-AR"],["to translate","traducir","trah-doo-SEER"],["to graduate","graduarse","grah-doo-AR-seh"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Spanish often drops the pronoun, because the verb ending already shows who is speaking."],"rows":[["I","yo","YOH"],["you (informal)","tú","too"],["he / she / you (formal)","él / ella / usted","ehl / EH-yah / oos-TEHD"],["we","nosotros","noh-SOH-trohs"],["you all (Spain)","vosotros","boh-SOH-trohs"],["they / you all","ellos / ustedes","EH-yohs / oos-TEH-dehs"]],"ex":[["I am a student","yo soy estudiante","yoh soy ehs-too-dee-AHN-teh"],["you are tall","tú eres alto","too EH-rehs AHL-toh"],["she is my sister","ella es mi hermana","EH-yah ehs mee ehr-MAH-nah"],["we are friends","nosotros somos amigos","noh-SOH-trohs SOH-mohs ah-MEE-gohs"],["they are teachers","ellos son profesores","EH-yohs sohn proh-feh-SOH-rehs"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Nouns are masculine or feminine. Most ending in -o are masculine, most ending in -a feminine. Learn the word with its article.","Plural: add -s after a vowel, -es after a consonant. Adjectives agree with the noun."],"rows":[["the (m / f)","el / la","ehl / lah"],["the (plural m / f)","los / las","lohs / lahs"],["a (m / f)","un / una","oon / OO-nah"]],"ex":[["the boy","el niño","ehl NEE-nyoh"],["the girl","la niña","lah NEE-nyah"],["the books","los libros","lohs LEE-brohs"],["a red house","una casa roja","OO-nah KAH-sah RROH-hah"],["the cities","las ciudades","lahs see-oo-DAH-dehs"],["one cat, two cats","un gato, dos gatos","oon GAH-toh dohs GAH-tohs"],["one pen, two pens","un bolígrafo, dos bolígrafos","oon boh-LEE-grah-foh dohs boh-LEE-grah-fohs"],["a lesson, lessons","una clase, clases","OO-nah KLAH-seh KLAH-sehs"]]},{"id":"ser-to-be-who-or-what","title":"Ser: to be (who or what)","text":["Use ser for identity, origin, jobs, descriptions and time. It is irregular."],"rows":[["I am","soy","soy"],["you are","eres","EH-rehs"],["he / she is","es","ehs"],["we are","somos","SOH-mohs"],["you all are (Spain)","sois","soys"],["they are","son","sohn"]],"ex":[["I am English","soy inglés","soy een-GLEHS"],["he is a doctor","él es médico","ehl ehs MEH-dee-koh"],["it is Monday","es lunes","ehs LOO-nehs"],["we are from Uzbekistan","somos de Uzbekistán","SOH-mohs deh ooz-beh-krees-TAHN"],["they are tall","son altos","sohn AHL-tohs"]]},{"id":"estar-to-be-where-or-how","title":"Estar: to be (where or how)","text":["Use estar for places and for feelings or conditions that change."],"rows":[["I am","estoy","ehs-TOY"],["you are","estás","ehs-TAHS"],["he / she is","está","ehs-TAH"],["we are","estamos","ehs-TAH-mohs"],["you all are (Spain)","estáis","ehs-TAYS"],["they are","están","ehs-TAHN"]],"ex":[["I am at home","estoy en casa","ehs-TOY ehn KAH-sah"],["she is tired","ella está cansada","EH-yah ehs-TAH kahn-SAH-dah"],["where are you?","¿dónde estás?","DOHN-deh ehs-TAHS"],["we are well","estamos bien","ehs-TAH-mohs bee-EHN"],["the soup is cold","la sopa está fría","lah SOH-pah ehs-TAH FREE-ah"]]},{"id":"tener-to-have","title":"Tener: to have","text":["Tener is also used for age (tengo 16 años) and for hunger, thirst and tiredness (tengo hambre, tengo sed, tengo sueño)."],"rows":[["I have","tengo","TEHN-goh"],["you have","tienes","tee-EH-nehs"],["he / she has","tiene","tee-EH-neh"],["we have","tenemos","teh-NEH-mohs"],["they have","tienen","tee-EH-nehn"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","tengo un hermano","TEHN-goh oon ehr-MAH-noh"],["she has two cats","ella tiene dos gatos","EH-yah tee-EH-neh dohs GAH-tohs"],["we have time","tenemos tiempo","teh-NEH-mohs tee-EHM-poh"],["I am hungry","tengo hambre","TEHN-goh AHM-breh"],["they have a car","tienen un coche","tee-EH-nehn oon KOH-cheh"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Take the ending off the infinitive, then add the new ending. Three families: -ar, -er, -ir."],"rows":[["hablar (to speak): yo","hablo","AH-bloh"],["tú","hablas","AH-blahs"],["él / ella","habla","AH-blah"],["nosotros","hablamos","ah-BLAH-mohs"],["ellos","hablan","AH-blahn"],["comer: yo, tú, él, nosotros, ellos","como, comes, come, comemos, comen","KOH-moh..."],["vivir: yo, tú, él, nosotros, ellos","vivo, vives, vive, vivimos, viven","BEE-boh..."]],"ex":[["I speak English","hablo inglés","AH-bloh een-GLEHS"],["you eat a lot","comes mucho","KOH-mehs MOO-choh"],["she lives in Madrid","ella vive en Madrid","EH-yah BEE-beh ehn mah-DREED"],["we work every day","trabajamos todos los días","trah-bah-HAH-mohs TOH-dohs lohs DEE-ahs"],["they drink water","beben agua","BEH-behn AH-gwah"]]},{"id":"ir-to-go","title":"Ir: to go","text":["To say you are going to do something: ir + a + infinitive. Voy a comer = I am going to eat."],"rows":[["I go","voy","boy"],["you go","vas","bahs"],["he / she goes","va","bah"],["we go","vamos","BAH-mohs"],["they go","van","bahn"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","voy al colegio","boy ahl koh-LEH-hee-oh"],["where are you going?","¿adónde vas?","ah-DOHN-deh bahs"],["we are going to eat","vamos a comer","BAH-mohs ah koh-MEHR"],["she is going to travel","ella va a viajar","EH-yah bah ah bee-ah-HAR"],["let's go!","¡vamos!","BAH-mohs"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Order: subject, verb, the rest. The adjective usually comes after the noun. You can drop the pronoun."],"rows":[["subject + verb + rest","Yo como pan.","yoh KOH-moh pahn"],["adjective after noun","una casa grande","OO-nah KAH-sah GRAHN-deh"],["add time or place at the end","Trabajo aquí hoy.","trah-BAH-hoh ah-KEE oy"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","como pan","KOH-moh pahn"],["Maria reads a book","María lee un libro","mah-REE-ah LEH-eh oon LEE-broh"],["we live in a big house","vivimos en una casa grande","bee-BEE-mohs ehn OO-nah KAH-sah GRAHN-deh"],["he works here today","él trabaja aquí hoy","ehl trah-BAH-hah ah-KEE oy"],["the dog is black","el perro es negro","ehl PEH-rroh ehs NEH-groh"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put no before the verb. Double negatives are normal: no tengo nada (I do not have anything).","Put no before the verb. Spanish uses double negatives: no tengo nada (I do not have anything)."],"rows":[["no + verb","no hablo","noh AH-bloh"],["nothing","nada","NAH-dah"],["nobody","nadie","NAH-dee-eh"],["never","nunca","NOON-kah"],["no + verb","no hablo","noh AH-bloh"],["nothing","nada","NAH-dah"],["nobody","nadie","NAH-dee-eh"],["never","nunca","NOON-kah"]],"ex":[["I want","quiero","kee-EH-roh"],["I do not want","no quiero","noh kee-EH-roh"],["I speak English","hablo inglés","AH-bloh een-GLEHS"],["I do not speak English","no hablo inglés","noh AH-bloh een-GLEHS"],["I like it","me gusta","meh GOOS-tah"],["I do not like it","no me gusta","noh meh GOOS-tah"],["she is here","ella está aquí","EH-yah ehs-TAH ah-KEE"],["she is not here","ella no está aquí","EH-yah noh ehs-TAH ah-KEE"],["I have a car","tengo coche","TEHN-goh KOH-cheh"],["I do not have a car","no tengo coche","noh TEHN-goh KOH-cheh"],["I understand","entiendo","ehn-tee-EHN-doh"],["I do not understand","no entiendo","noh ehn-tee-EHN-doh"],["we are tired","estamos cansados","ehs-TAH-mohs kahn-SAH-dohs"],["we are not tired","no estamos cansados","noh ehs-TAH-mohs kahn-SAH-dohs"],["he works on Sundays","trabaja los domingos","trah-BAH-hah lohs doh-MEEN-gohs"],["he does not work on Sundays","no trabaja los domingos","noh trah-BAH-hah lohs doh-MEEN-gohs"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Yes or no question: same words as a statement, with a rising voice and ¿ ?. Often the subject goes after the verb."],"rows":[["statement","Tú hablas inglés.","too AH-blahs een-GLEHS"],["question","¿Hablas inglés?","AH-blahs een-GLEHS"],["add \"right?\"","¿verdad?","behr-DAHD"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","¿hablas inglés?","AH-blahs een-GLEHS"],["is she a doctor?","¿es médica?","ehs MEH-dee-kah"],["do you have a pen?","¿tienes un bolígrafo?","tee-EH-nehs oon boh-LEE-grah-foh"],["are you tired?","¿estás cansado?","ehs-TAHS kahn-SAH-doh"],["is it far?","¿está lejos?","ehs-TAH LEH-hohs"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","qué","keh"],["who","quién","kee-EHN"],["where","dónde","DOHN-deh"],["when","cuándo","KWAHN-doh"],["why","por qué","pohr KEH"],["how","cómo","KOH-moh"],["which","cuál","kwahl"],["how much / how many","cuánto / cuántos","KWAHN-toh / KWAHN-tohs"]],"ex":[["what is this?","¿qué es esto?","keh ehs EHS-toh"],["who is she?","¿quién es ella?","kee-EHN ehs EH-yah"],["where do you live?","¿dónde vives?","DOHN-deh BEE-behs"],["when is the exam?","¿cuándo es el examen?","KWAHN-doh ehs ehl ehk-SAH-mehn"],["why are you late?","¿por qué llegas tarde?","pohr KEH YEH-gahs TAR-deh"],["how much is it?","¿cuánto cuesta?","KWAHN-toh KWEHS-tah"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["To say you like something, use gustar: me gusta (one thing), me gustan (several things)."],"rows":[["my","mi / mis","mee / mees"],["your","tu / tus","too / toos"],["his / her","su / sus","soo / soos"],["our","nuestro","NWEHS-troh"]],"ex":[["my house","mi casa","mee KAH-sah"],["your friends","tus amigos","toos ah-MEE-gohs"],["I like coffee","me gusta el café","meh GOOS-tah ehl kah-FEH"],["I like dogs","me gustan los perros","meh GOOS-tahn lohs PEH-rrohs"],["she likes music","le gusta la música","leh GOOS-tah lah MOO-see-kah"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Informal: tú (one person), vosotros (several, Spain). Formal: usted and ustedes, with the verb in the he / she form."],"rows":[["you, informal","tú","too"],["you, formal","usted","oos-TEHD"],["you all, informal (Spain)","vosotros","boh-SOH-trohs"],["you all, formal","ustedes","oos-TEH-dehs"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","tú hablas","too AH-blahs"],["you speak (formal)","usted habla","oos-TEHD AH-blah"],["you are tired (informal)","estás cansado","ehs-TAHS kahn-SAH-doh"],["you are tired (formal)","está cansado","ehs-TAH kahn-SAH-doh"],["your name (formal)","su nombre","soo NOHM-breh"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past (preterite) of -ar verbs: -é, -aste, -ó, -amos, -aron. Future: infinitive + -é, -ás, -á, -emos, -án."],"rows":[["I spoke","hablé","ah-BLEH"],["you spoke","hablaste","ah-BLAHS-teh"],["he / she spoke","habló","ah-BLOH"],["I will speak","hablaré","ah-blah-REH"],["we will speak","hablaremos","ah-blah-REH-mohs"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","ayer trabajé","ah-YEHR trah-bah-HEH"],["she bought a book","ella compró un libro","EH-yah kohm-PROH oon LEE-broh"],["I will call you tomorrow","te llamaré mañana","teh yah-mah-REH mah-NYAH-nah"],["we will eat at eight","comeremos a las ocho","koh-meh-REH-mohs ah lahs OH-choh"],["they travelled to Spain","viajaron a España","bee-ah-HAH-rohn ah ehs-PAH-nyah"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal (tú): use the él form for -ar / -er / -ir verbs (habla, come, escribe). Negative: no + the -es / -as form (no hables). Formal (usted): hable, coma."],"rows":[["speak! (informal)","¡habla!","AH-blah"],["do not speak!","¡no hables!","noh AH-blehs"],["speak! (formal)","¡hable!","AH-bleh"]],"ex":[["come here","ven aquí","behn ah-KEE"],["do not come here","no vengas aquí","noh BEHN-gahs ah-KEE"],["sit down","siéntate","see-EHN-tah-teh"],["do not sit down","no te sientes","noh teh see-EHN-tehs"],["be quiet","cállate","KAH-yah-teh"],["do not be late","no llegues tarde","noh YEH-gehs TAR-deh"],["open the door","abre la puerta","AH-breh lah PWEHR-tah"],["close the window","cierra la ventana","see-EH-rrah lah behn-TAH-nah"],["listen to me","escúchame","ehs-KOO-chah-meh"],["do not worry","no te preocupes","noh teh preh-oh-KOO-pehs"],["speak slowly","habla despacio","AH-blah dehs-PAH-see-oh"],["wait a moment","espera un momento","ehs-PEH-rah oon moh-MEHN-toh"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["poder (can), deber / tener que (must), querer (want) + infinitive: puedo nadar, tengo que ir, quiero comer. No tiene que = it is not necessary; no debes = you must not."],"rows":[["I can","puedo","PWEH-doh"],["I must","tengo que","TEHN-goh keh"],["I want","quiero","kee-EH-roh"]],"ex":[["I can swim","puedo nadar","PWEH-doh nah-DAR"],["I cannot swim","no puedo nadar","noh PWEH-doh nah-DAR"],["can you help me?","¿puedes ayudarme?","PWEH-dehs ah-yoo-DAR-meh"],["we must go","tenemos que irnos","teh-NEH-mohs keh EER-nohs"],["we must not go","no debemos irnos","noh deh-BEH-mohs EER-nohs"],["I want to eat","quiero comer","kee-EH-roh koh-MEHR"],["I do not want to eat","no quiero comer","noh kee-EH-roh koh-MEHR"],["you can come","puedes venir","PWEH-dehs beh-NEER"],["you cannot come","no puedes venir","noh PWEH-dehs beh-NEER"],["she wants to study","ella quiere estudiar","EH-yah kee-EH-reh ehs-too-dee-AR"],["I must work today","tengo que trabajar hoy","TEHN-goh keh trah-bah-HAR oy"],["you must not run","no debes correr","noh DEH-behs koh-RREHR"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["en = in / on / at. debajo de = under, encima de = on top of, al lado de = next to, cerca de = near, a las nueve = at nine."],"rows":[["in / on / at","en","ehn"],["under","debajo de","deh-BAH-hoh deh"],["next to","al lado de","ahl LAH-doh deh"],["near","cerca de","SEHR-kah deh"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","el libro está encima de la mesa","ehl LEE-broh ehs-TAH ehn-SEE-mah deh lah MEH-sah"],["the cat is under the table","el gato está debajo de la mesa","ehl GAH-toh ehs-TAH deh-BAH-hoh deh lah MEH-sah"],["I am at school","estoy en el colegio","ehs-TOY ehn ehl koh-LEH-hee-oh"],["I am at home","estoy en casa","ehs-TOY ehn KAH-sah"],["the shop is next to the bank","la tienda está al lado del banco","lah tee-EHN-dah ehs-TAH ahl LAH-doh dehl BAHN-koh"],["the park is near the station","el parque está cerca de la estación","ehl PAR-keh ehs-TAH SEHR-kah deh lah ehs-tah-see-OHN"],["we meet in the morning","nos vemos por la mañana","nohs BEH-mohs pohr lah mah-NYAH-nah"],["the lesson is at nine","la clase es a las nueve","lah KLAH-seh ehs ah lahs NWEH-beh"],["the key is in the bag","la llave está en la bolsa","lah YAH-beh ehs-TAH ehn lah BOHL-sah"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["más + adjective + que = more than (más grande que). menos... que = less than. el más... = the most. mejor = better, peor = worse."],"rows":[["bigger than","más grande que","mahs GRAHN-deh keh"],["better","mejor","meh-HOR"],["the biggest","el más grande","ehl mahs GRAHN-deh"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","grande, más grande, el más grande","GRAHN-deh mahs GRAHN-deh ehl mahs GRAHN-deh"],["small, smaller, the smallest","pequeño, más pequeño, el más pequeño","peh-KEH-nyoh mahs peh-KEH-nyoh ehl mahs peh-KEH-nyoh"],["this is better than that","esto es mejor que eso","EHS-toh ehs meh-HOR keh EH-soh"],["this is worse than that","esto es peor que eso","EHS-toh ehs peh-OR keh EH-soh"],["she is taller than me","ella es más alta que yo","EH-yah ehs mahs AHL-tah keh yoh"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Taskent es más grande que Samarcanda","tahsh-KEHNT ehs mahs GRAHN-deh keh sah-mar-KAHN-dah"],["it is the cheapest","es el más barato","ehs ehl mahs bah-RAH-toh"],["the same as","igual que","ee-GWAHL keh"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","él es profesor","ehl ehs proh-feh-SOHR"],["you (plural) are students","vosotros sois estudiantes","boh-SOH-trohs soys ehs-too-dee-AHN-tehs"],["I am happy","estoy contento","ehs-TOY kohn-TEHN-toh"],["she is at school","ella está en el colegio","EH-yah ehs-TAH ehn ehl koh-LEH-hee-oh"],["you are my friend","eres mi amigo","EH-rehs mee ah-MEE-goh"],["it is cold","hace frío","AH-seh FREE-oh"],["I study English","estudio inglés","ehs-TOO-dee-oh een-GLEHS"],["he teaches maths","enseña matemáticas","ehn-SEH-nyah mah-teh-MAH-tee-kahs"],["they work every day","trabajan todos los días","trah-BAH-hahn TOH-dohs lohs DEE-ahs"],["is this your book?","¿es este tu libro?","ehs EHS-teh too LEE-broh"],["are they here?","¿están aquí?","ehs-TAHN ah-KEE"],["do you like tea?","¿te gusta el té?","teh GOOS-tah ehl teh"],["what time is it?","¿qué hora es?","keh OH-rah ehs"],["whose book is this?","¿de quién es este libro?","deh kee-EHN ehs EHS-teh LEE-broh"],["how old are you?","¿cuántos años tienes?","KWAHN-tohs AH-nyohs tee-EH-nehs"],["how do you say it?","¿cómo se dice?","KOH-moh seh DEE-seh"],["your book (formal)","su libro","soo LEE-broh"],["their house","su casa","soo KAH-sah"],["my phone","mi móvil","mee MOH-beel"],["excuse me, sir","disculpe, señor","dees-KOOL-peh seh-NYOR"],["please sit down (formal)","siéntese, por favor","see-EHN-teh-seh pohr fah-BOR"],["come here (informal)","ven aquí","behn ah-KEE"],["yesterday I was tired","ayer estaba cansado","ah-YEHR ehs-TAH-bah kahn-SAH-doh"],["I will study tomorrow","estudiaré mañana","ehs-too-dee-ah-REH mah-NYAH-nah"],["we went to the park","fuimos al parque","FWEE-mohs ahl PAR-keh"]]}],"name":"Spanish","id":"es","flag":"es","note":""}